<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47685" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦχος</span></b> , ὁ, later form
		of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχή</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Arist.
			<u>Aud.</u>
			804a30
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Theoc.
			27.57
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Ep.Hebr.</u>
			12.19
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Ael.
			<u>Tact.</u>
			35.3
		</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεττίγων λιγὺν ἦ</span>. <i><span class="en">
			Call.
			<u>Aet.Oxy.</u>
			2079.29
		</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧχον</span> Pap.); <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παγᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mosch.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					1.12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.98
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ τῶν πριόνων ἦχοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Synt.</u>
					290.24
				</span></i>
			; of the <i>sound</i> of words, opp. sense, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.258S.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦχοι καὶ ψόφοι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.150S.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς φωνῆς ὁ ἦ. ἐν ταῖς ἀκοαῖς
					παραμένει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Nigr.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γραμμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Demetr.
					<u>Eloc.</u>
					71
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ. ἐν ὠσί</span>, or abs.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦχοι, ἦχος</span>, <i>ringing in
				the ears</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Coac.</u>
				189
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				190
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Prorrh.</u>
				1.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Sens.</u>
				19
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦχοι ὤτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SA</u>
					1.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>echo</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				899b30
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> Gramm.,
				<i>breathing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦχοι ὁ μὲν δασύς, ὁ δὲ ψιλός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Demetr.
					<u>Eloc.</u>
					73
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>voice</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἦ. εὔτονον καὶ λαμπρὸν ἀποτελεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					5.17
				</span></i>
			. (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦχος</span></b> , τό, is found in <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Je.</u>
				28(51).16
			</span></i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				21.25
			</span></i>.)</div>
